cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BL127 or BL19, please cite it as below."
title: "Blockulator: BL127 and BL19, high-precision math for the EVM"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Secure Data Research, LLC"
    website: "https://securedataresearch.net"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/securedataresearch/blockulator"
url: "https://blockulator.com"
abstract: >-
  Two math libraries for the EVM in which every op is exact or rounds once.
  BL127 is signed 127.128 fixed point: 38 digits at 1 and a range of
  ±1.7 × 10^38, in 53 ops. BL19 is a 256-bit binary float: about 71 digits at
  any magnitude from about 10^-78,913 to about 10^78,913, in 65 ops, the special
  functions among them. Both ship as deployed contracts with no owner and as
  inline libraries.
version: "3.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
keywords:
  - ethereum
  - evm
  - fixed-point
  - floating-point
  - solidity
  - yul
